      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{5} & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $1$st *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{5} & -6 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1+\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-6)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 7\\cdot 1+(-8)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/id": "51b920b8-cedd-511f-b44b-e17af25cb60d",
